Type-1 (Identical): Exact duplicates with only whitespace and comment differences.
Type-2 (Parameterized): Structurally identical with variations in identifiers, literals, or types. 
Type-3 (Gapped): Similar structure with added, deleted, or modified statements. 
Type-4 (Semantic): Different syntax but equivalent functionality.

Type-1 Example:
// Clone 1
int sum = a + b;
return sum;

// Clone 2
int sum=a+b;
return sum;

Type-2 Example:
// Clone 1
int calculateArea(int width, int height) {
    return width * height;
}

// Clone 2
int computeArea(int w, int h) {
    return w * h;
}

Type-3 Example:
// Clone 1
if (x > 0) {
    result = x * 2;
    return result;
}

// Clone 2
if (y > 0) {
    System.out.println("Processing...");
    result = y * 2;
    return result;
}

Type-4 Example:
// Clone 1
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    sum += arr[i];
}

// Clone 2
int i = 0;
while (i < arr.length) {
    sum += arr[i];
    i++;
}

